# Product Requirements Documents

One file per feature / initiative. Living docs — update as scope clarifies, archive when shipped.

## File naming

`<slug>.md` — e.g. `search-v2.md`, `oauth-migration.md`. No numbering required.

## Template

```markdown
# PRD: <feature>

- **Status**: Draft | Review | Approved | Shipped | Cancelled
- **Owner**: <name>
- **Last updated**: YYYY-MM-DD

## Goal

One sentence: what user problem does this solve?

## Non-goals

What this explicitly does NOT do. Bound the scope.

## User stories

- As a <role>, I want <action> so that <outcome>.
- …

## Success metrics

How will we know it worked? Concrete, measurable.

## Constraints

Tech, time, compliance, dependency constraints.

## Open questions

Decisions still needed. Move to a Decisions section once resolved (or split into ADRs).

## Linked artifacts

- Design / mockups
- Related ADRs
- Tracking issue / ticket
```

## Workflow

1. Draft a PRD before substantial implementation work.
2. Spawn ADRs from open questions as design decisions get made.
3. On ship, update Status, leave the file as a historical artifact.

PRDs answer "what + why". ADRs answer "how + why we chose this how".
